# ResearchGoblin should be correspondingly narrow

I wouldn't call it `ArxivGoblin`, because arXiv is only one source.

Something like:

```text
ResearchGoblin
├── arXiv
├── OpenAlex
├── conference proceedings
├── lab publication feeds
├── author histories
├── citations
├── datasets
├── benchmarks
└── possibly research blogs
```

OpenAlex is useful specifically because its scholarly graph gives you structured works/authors/relationships rather than just an arXiv feed; its dataset is explicitly structured around scholarly entities and relations that can be queried or locally loaded. ([OpenAlex][3])

Its ontology could be:

