# And the opposite direction is equally useful

GitGoblin may discover something **before academia describes it clearly**.

```text
GitGoblin
 detects 7 unrelated agent frameworks
 adopting similar checkpoint pattern
             │
             ▼
Primitive:
"transactional agent checkpointing"
             │
             ▼
ResearchGoblin
 search papers / methods
             │
       ┌─────┴─────┐
       │           │
 known theory    little theory
       │           │
       ▼           ▼
 correlate     emerging practice
```

So you get both:

```text
THEORY → CODE
```

and:

```text
CODE → THEORY
```

That makes the combined intelligence graph much stronger.

