# The object that joins everything should be `Technique`

I wouldn't join paper directly to repo.

Use:

```text
                    Technique
                   /         \
                  /           \
             Paper             Repo
               │                │
             claims         implements
               │                │
               ▼                ▼
            Result          Capability
```

For example:

```text
Technique:
    speculative decoding

Papers:
    P1
    P2
    P3

Implementations:
    repo A @ commit X
    repo B @ release Y

Capabilities:
    inference.latency.reduce

Benchmarks:
    benchmark B

Evidence:
    ...
```

Then a paper can be wrong without invalidating the technique identity, and one repo can implement several techniques.

This is exactly the kind of identity/interpretation separation you already learned from Pāṭala.

